From: FoAKTEE <hw609@cantab.ac.uk>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:19:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/24] perf(m12-openmp): trace every pixel in one OpenMP loop
 with phase timers

- change: calculate_image_all runs the per-pixel body of calculate_image_block over all blocks in one parallel for (dynamic, 64) instead of one 100-pixel region per block (AMR keeps the block loop); main reports RAPTOR_TIMERS (load, setup, loop, output walls; thread-summed geodesic and transfer times; rays, stored states)
- change: under STEP_BBH the HDF5 image carries endclass (1/2 captured by hole 1/2, 3 escaped, 4 budget, 5 non-finite) and nsamples per pixel
- verify: R01 synthetic image (bhac, CKS, pol, switches off) bitwise identical to upstream b91e937 in I, Q, U, V, tau, tauF, alpha, beta and the spectrum
---
 src/core.c      | 78 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/functions.h | 17 +++++++++++
 src/io.c        | 21 +++++++++++++
 src/main.c      | 29 ++++++++++++++++--
 4 files changed, 142 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

